# The repository root .gitignore has a bare `data/` pattern (under "#Database files"), which
# matches a directory named `data` at ANY depth — including infra/terraform/modules/data/.
# Without this negation the entire data module, RDS and the two-database-user bootstrap
# included, is silently absent from git: `git add` reports nothing and the working tree looks
# complete.
#
# Re-included as a DIRECTORY rather than as a file glob, because gitignore cannot re-include
# a path whose parent directory is still excluded.
#
# The broader fix belongs in the root .gitignore — `data/` should be anchored (`/data/`)
# rather than matching at any depth, since otherwise it will do this again to any future
# `data` directory in any package. Out of scope for OB-007, which owns infra/ only.
!terraform/modules/data/
